[02:22.42] Now in this far away land
[02:28.78] Strange that the palms of my hands
[02:33.75] Should be damp with expectancy
[03:49.61] Spring, and the air's turning mild
[03:56.23] City lights and the glimpse of a child
[04:01.41] Of the alleyway infantry
[04:08.57] Friends, do they know what I mean?
[04:15.09] Rain and the gathering green
[04:20.19] Of an afternoon out of town
[04:28.49] But Lord I had to go
[04:31.62] The trail was laid too slow behind me
[04:36.83] To face the call of fame
[04:40.58] Or make a drunkard's name for me
[04:46.25] Though now this better life
[04:50.25] Has brought a different understanding
[04:56.20] And from these endless days
[05:00.19] Shall come a broader sympathy
[05:06.02] And though I count the hours
[05:10.29] To be alone's no injury
[05:15.45] My home was a place by the sand
[05:21.73] Cliffs and a military band
[05:26.91] Blew an air of normality
[05:35.32] 